WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:15.286
"Can you really fix my bike?"

2
00:00:15.666 --> 00:00:16.826
Nathan asked Tina.

3
00:00:16.846 --> 00:00:19.748
"Thanks!" "You're welcome.

4
00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:21.768
This will only take a second."

5
00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:27.191
Tina bent over the bike and expertly put the chain back in place.

6
00:00:28.011 --> 00:00:29.652
Then she turned the pedals to test it.

7
00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.705
"Good as new," she said.

8
00:00:32.725 --> 00:00:34.686
"It should be fine now."

9
00:00:34.706 --> 00:00:36.547
"Thank you so much!"

10
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:37.768
Nathan exclaimed.

11
00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:39.769
"I really appreciate it."

12
00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:42.571
"No problem.

13
00:00:43.211 --> 00:00:44.592
Enjoy the rest of the ride!"

14
00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.594
With a friendly wave to all of them, Tina pedaled off.

15
00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:52.376
"Wow," Maggie said.

16
00:00:52.396 --> 00:00:54.417
"That was really nice of her."

17
00:00:55.358 --> 00:00:56.038
Cole nodded.

18
00:00:56.058 --> 00:00:59.500
"Yeah, and she's one of our suspects," he said.

19
00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:04.178
"Would someone who just slashed a bunch of tires do something nice like that?"

20
00:01:04.198 --> 00:01:09.200
"I'm glad you guys are trying to figure out who slashed those tires," Nathan said.

21
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.601
"That means it won't be long until the mystery is solved.

22
00:01:13.482 --> 00:01:16.083
The Lemonade Detectives solve all their cases!"

23
00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:19.384
He rode off, humming happily.

24
00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.326
Henry frowned, realizing that Nathan was right.

25
00:01:22.346 --> 00:01:24.827
"It's true," he said.

26
00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:27.588
"We've solved every case so far.

27
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.641
But this one might be our toughest yet."

28
00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.602
Maggie looked worried.

29
00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:33.802
"You're right.

30
00:01:34.523 --> 00:01:36.844
What if we can't solve it before the ride is over?

31
00:01:37.804 --> 00:01:40.565
The Lemonade Detectives' reputation will be ruined!"

32
00:01:40.585 --> 00:01:44.627
"And so will the soccer team's fundraiser," Cole said.

33
00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:46.268
"But don't worry.

34
00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:49.929
We already have it narrowed down to three suspects, remember?"

35
00:01:49.949 --> 00:01:53.011
"Or maybe two," Henry said.

36
00:01:53.031 --> 00:01:56.052
"It's hard to believe Tina is the culprit.

37
00:01:56.784 --> 00:01:57.925
She seems too nice.

38
00:01:59.065 --> 00:02:03.447
And she seemed pretty mad when she accused Joey of slashing the tires earlier."

39
00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:06.908
"But why would she help raise money for Belltown?"

40
00:02:07.268 --> 00:02:07.909
Maggie said.

41
00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:09.749
"That doesn't make sense."

42
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.671
"I don't know," Henry said.

43
00:02:12.691 --> 00:02:16.032
"But I know someone who might be able to tell us.

44
00:02:17.012 --> 00:02:21.454
I just remembered I saw Tina sitting with Daisy for a while during the break."

45
00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:25.236
"Oh yeah, I noticed that too," Cole said.

46
00:02:26.152 --> 00:02:30.936
"I was surprised that Tina wasn't sitting with that Joey guy since they're both from Valley High.

47
00:02:31.657 --> 00:02:33.618
Do you think Tina and Daisy are friends?"

48
00:02:34.559 --> 00:02:37.341
"There's only one way to find out," Henry replied.

49
00:02:37.361 --> 00:02:39.303
"Let's go ask Daisy."

50
00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:42.866
They rode ahead until they caught up with Daisy.

51
00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:49.091
Maggie jumped right into questioning her.

52
00:02:49.111 --> 00:02:53.855
"We saw you sitting with that girl from Valley High earlier," she said to Daisy.

53
00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:55.216
"Do you know her?"

54
00:02:56.224 --> 00:02:57.265
"You mean Tina?"

55
00:02:57.545 --> 00:02:58.285
Daisy nodded.

56
00:02:58.305 --> 00:03:01.207
"We went to the same summer camp last year.

57
00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:02.748
She's cool."

58
00:03:02.768 --> 00:03:05.189
"Is that why she came on this ride?"

59
00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:06.210
Cole asked.

60
00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.951
"Because you two are friends?"

61
00:03:08.951 --> 00:03:09.752
Daisy shrugged.

62
00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:12.553
"I'm the one who told her about the fundraiser.

63
00:03:13.414 --> 00:03:15.895
But she probably would have heard about it anyway.

64
00:03:16.736 --> 00:03:18.496
She's a really serious rider.

65
00:03:19.177 --> 00:03:24.440
She trains all the time, and she enters every local ride and race she can find."

66
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.001
"Oh, that explains why she's here!"

67
00:03:28.321 --> 00:03:28.941
Henry said.

68
00:03:28.961 --> 00:03:32.502
"It also explains how she knew how to fix Nathan's bike."

69
00:03:32.522 --> 00:03:35.323
"Wait a minute," Daisy said.

70
00:03:35.343 --> 00:03:39.264
"You don't suspect Tina of slashing those tires, do you?

71
00:03:40.184 --> 00:03:42.345
Because she'd never do something like that.

72
00:03:43.065 --> 00:03:46.006
She loves bikes, plus she's really nice."

73
00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.067
"Yeah. We just figured that out."

74
00:03:49.407 --> 00:03:50.327
Henry smiled.

75
00:03:50.347 --> 00:03:51.607
"Don't worry.

76
00:03:52.247 --> 00:03:54.028
She's off our list of suspects."

77
00:03:55.052 --> 00:03:57.514
He, Maggie, and Cole rode off by themselves.

78
00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:02.537
"So now we only have two suspects," Cole said.

79
00:04:02.557 --> 00:04:05.139
"William and the mystery man."

80
00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:09.862
"Both of them have been acting suspicious all day," Maggie said.

81
00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:13.685
"But neither has a good motive," Henry pointed out.

82
00:04:13.705 --> 00:04:16.327
"At least not one we know about."

83
00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:20.410
"William isn't having much fun on this ride," Maggie said.

84
00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.312
"He acts like he doesn't even want to be here."

85
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.800
"And he tried to convince Ms.

86
00:04:25.841 --> 00:04:29.482
Hernandez to let him quit at the first rest break," Cole said.

87
00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:35.083
"Maybe he slashed the tires because he thought the rest of the ride would be canceled.

88
00:04:36.484 --> 00:04:39.985
Then when it wasn't, he had to figure out another way to quit early."

89
00:04:40.005 --> 00:04:43.966
"Why would he come on the ride at all if he didn't want to be here?"

90
00:04:44.346 --> 00:04:45.106
Maggie wondered.

91
00:04:45.126 --> 00:04:47.827
"Do you think his parents made him come?"

92
00:04:47.847 --> 00:04:50.528
"I don't know," Henry said.

93
00:04:51.432 --> 00:04:56.055
"But I can't stop thinking about how that guy lied to us about being a reporter.

94
00:04:56.875 --> 00:04:58.096
Why would he do that?"

95
00:04:58.116 --> 00:05:01.078
"Good question," Maggie said.

96
00:05:01.098 --> 00:05:03.860
"I just don't know how we're going to figure it out.

97
00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.321
He won't tell us anything.

98
00:05:07.082 --> 00:05:09.143
And nobody else here knows anything about him."

99
00:05:11.304 --> 00:05:13.205
Soon they reached the next rest area.

100
00:05:14.966 --> 00:05:17.328
Henry coasted to a stop behind the other bikes.

101
00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:22.185
This picnic area was right beside a parking lot.

102
00:05:24.086 --> 00:05:28.069
That was good since it meant that nobody could touch the bikes without being seen.

103
00:05:28.089 --> 00:05:32.171
"We'd better figure out how to solve this case," Henry said.

104
00:05:32.191 --> 00:05:34.092
"We're almost out of time."
